From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 43/92] lower independent queues' render calls on a bounded set
 of lanes

RenderLoweringPolicy::Worker lowered every queue's logged render calls on one
thread per device, so busy Sims (one queue each, one VkDevice) serialized there.
The device now lowers on up to lanes() threads (one per 4 host threads, 1..4).
Each command queue takes a lane in turn at creation and keeps it; its slots are
handed only to that lane, so one queue's slots are lowered one at a time in hand
order as before. Only different lanes run at once, as AtCall's program threads
of different queues already do. A lane's thread starts with its first slot.

Unchanged: one device-wide QueuedCommits order and its single runner (binary
semaphores and events of a later commit never pass an earlier one), slot
ownership (queued/busy/draining), drains and settle. Per lane: the queue, its
park/wake and the ENDS_IN_FLIGHT bound (no cross-Sim back-pressure). A panic on
any lane, or a lane thread that fails to start, ends every lane: queued slots
are left to their programs' drains, the lost slot refuses later drains. Teardown
stops and joins every started lane (not one on its own thread). A kept slot
still queued on another lane is not reused for an encoder of a different lane.

Test (lavapipe, m2v_cpu_icd): two queues on different lanes, queue A's slot
held so its lane waits inside it: queue B's batches and end are lowered while
B's commit stays behind A's; a cross-queue event gates B's copy; pixels, word,
per-queue handler order and status equal AtCall; a refused commit on A still
lets A's signal and B complete; a work-counts drain with both lanes busy
returns; teardown joins both. Negative control (all queues on lane 0) fails at
the overlap check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
